From daac7047cb83ceeb4ef284b9ddbeecc488e5c662 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:16:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/52] Test KiCad schematic support against further KiCad
 versions

Upstream's schematic tests only use the schematics of one KiCad
version, 9.0.6. The new kicad_extra_source_revisions setting lists
further versions, by tag or commit, whose demo and QA schematics are
tested as well. Of these, only the schematics are fetched, from a
sparse checkout of KiCad's repository without history. The
KICAD_EXTRA_SOURCES environment variable overrides them with local
checkouts.

The first further version is KiCad 10.0.8, with 424 schematics. The
demo schematics in subdirectories of KiCad's demos directory are tested
too, in all versions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013wvKon1yvwjNtAdtSuZzZh
